---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const pageTitle =
  "A&DS S01E01. Algorithms. Time complexity. Merge sort.";
const unit = "1.1";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  unit={unit}
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">
    {pageTitle}
  </h1>
  <hr class="mb-6" />

  <!-- 1.1 Algorithms Time Complexity -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
      >1.1 For each algorithm below,
      calculate its time complexity</summary
    >

    <h2>a)</h2>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-python">
for i in range(n):
    j = 0
    while j * j &lt; i:
        j += 1
# Solution:
# Inner loop: j &lt; sqrt(i) → O(sqrt(i))
# Total: sum O(sqrt(i)) from i=0..n ≈ O(n^(3/2))
    </code></pre>

    <h2>b)</h2>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-python">
for i in range(n):
    j = i
    while j &gt; 0:
        j = j // 2
# Solution:
# Inner loop: O(log i)
# Total sum over i=1..n → O(n log n)
    </code></pre>

    <h2>c)</h2>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-python">
def f(n):
    if n == 0:
        return 1
    else:
        return 5 * f(n // 3)
# Solution:
# Recurrence: T(n) = T(n/3) + O(1)
# Time complexity: O(log n)
    </code></pre>

    <h2>d)</h2>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-python">
def f(n):
    if n == 0:
        return 1
    else:
        return f(n // 3) + f(n // 3)
# Solution:
# Recurrence: T(n) = 2*T(n/3) + O(1)
# Time complexity: O(n^log3(2)) ≈ O(n^0.63)
    </code></pre>
  </details>

  <!-- 1.2 Induction Proofs -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
      >1.2 – 1.5 Time complexity proofs
      using induction</summary
    >

    <h2>
      1.2 Prove T(n) = 2T(n/2) + n ⇒
      T(n) = Ω(n log n)
    </h2>
    <p>
      Solution: Base case: n = 1 → T(1)
      = 1<br />
      Induction hypothesis: Assume T(k) ≥
      c k log k for k &lt; n<br />
      Inductive step:
      <br />
      T(n) = 2 T(n/2) + n ≥ 2 * c * (n/2)
      * log(n/2) + n = c n log n - c n + n
      → choose c ≤ 1<br />
      ✅ Conclusion: T(n) = Ω(n log n)
    </p>

    <h2>
      1.3 Prove T(n) = 2T(n/2 + 20) + n
      ⇒ T(n) = O(n log n)
    </h2>
    <p>
      Solution: +20 does not change
      asymptotics; recursive expansion
      yields O(n log n)
    </p>

    <h2>
      1.4 Prove T(n) = log n · T(n / log
      n) + n ⇒ T(n) = O(n log n)
    </h2>
    <p>
      Solution: Each recursion reduces
      problem size multiplicatively;
      logarithmic factor multiplies log
      n times → total O(n log n)
    </p>

    <h2>
      1.5 Prove T(n) = 2T(√n) + 1 ⇒ T(n)
      = O(log n)
    </h2>
    <p>
      Solution: Let n = 2^k → S(k) = 2
      S(k/2) + 1 → solves to O(k) =
      O(log n)
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- 1.6 – 1.10 Arrays problems -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
      >1.6 – 1.10 Array tasks</summary
    >

    <h2>
      1.6 Determine if a number occurs
      in both arrays (sorted)
    </h2>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-python">
i = j = 0
while i &lt; len(a) and j &lt; len(b):
    if a[i] == b[j]:
        return True
    elif a[i] &lt; b[j]:
        i += 1
    else:
        j += 1
# Complexity: O(n)
    </code></pre>

    <h2>
      1.7 Find i,j such that |ai - bj|
      is minimal
    </h2>
    <p>
      Two-pointer approach, advance
      pointer of smaller element → O(n)
    </p>

    <h2>
      1.8 Find i,j such that ai + bj = S
    </h2>
    <p>
      Two-pointer: start at a[0], b[-1],
      move left/right to adjust sum →
      O(n)
    </p>

    <h2>
      1.9 Count pairs i,j such that ai =
      bj
    </h2>
    <p>
      Two-pointer approach counting
      duplicates → O(n)
    </p>

    <h2>
      1.10 Count pairs i,j such that ai
      &gt; bj
    </h2>
    <p>
      Two-pointer, increment count when
      a[i] &gt; b[j] → O(n)
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- 1.11 Inversions -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
      >1.11 Count inversions in an array</summary
    >
    <p>
      Solution: Use merge sort; while
      merging, count elements remaining
      in left array when taking from
      right → O(n log n)
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- 1.12 – 1.14 Merge sort -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
      >1.12 – 1.14 Merge sort tasks</summary
    >

    <h2>
      1.12 Show merge sort is stable
    </h2>
    <p>
      Solution: Pick left element before
      right when equal during merge →
      preserves order → stable
    </p>

    <h2>
      1.13 Merge sort using single
      auxiliary array
    </h2>
    <p>
      Solution: Allocate tmp[n] once and
      reuse during all merges → memory
      efficient
    </p>

    <h2>
      1.14 Merge sort without recursion
    </h2>
    <p>
      Solution: Iterative bottom-up
      merge sort: merge subarrays of
      size 1, 2, 4… doubling each step →
      O(n log n)
    </p>
  </details>
</BaseLayout>
